What happens when a kobold zaps a wand of wishing?  Or create monster?
Do the monster's attack you or the kobold?

It would get very interesting if nethack could treat every moster in the
game the same way you were.  I would like to see nethack go object
oriented, where everything alive is a "monster" and everything dead is a
"an object".  Everything with a given letter would be of the same class,
and specific types of a given letter would be a method on that class:

// A C++ example of an orc class.
class orc : public monster {
	orc();
	orc~();
	captain(); // Creates an orc captain
	hill();	   // Creates a hill orc;
	...
}	

This could make a very intersting game.  You would be created as
character of your type which is a subclass of human (or elf).  This would
also make it easier to make a Dwarf or Ogre a player class.  Of course
each monster object might require more memory, but would do away with the
god aweful arrays of monsters and objects.

Unfortunately I don't have the time to volunteer for this effort :-(

